          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef mreach_mst_and_eom(X, k: int, lam_birth: float, lam_deaths_parent, lam_deaths_children) -> tuple[float, float, bool]:\n    X = np.asarray(X, dtype=float)\n    n = X.shape[0]\n    D = np.sqrt(np.sum((X[:, None, :] - X[None, :, :]) ** 2, axis=2))\n    core_d = np.partition(D, kth=k - 1, axis=1)[:, k - 1]\n    M = np.maximum(np.maximum(core_d[:, None], core_d[None, :]), D)\n    np.fill_diagonal(M, 0.0)\n    in_tree = np.zeros(n, dtype=bool)\n    min_e = np.full(n, np.inf)\n    min_e[0] = 0.0\n    mst_w = 0.0\n    for _ in range(n):\n        u = int(np.argmin(np.where(in_tree, np.inf, min_e)))\n        in_tree[u] = True\n        mst_w += float(min_e[u])\n        mask = (~in_tree) & (M[u] < min_e)\n        min_e[mask] = M[u, mask]\n    s_parent = float(np.sum(np.asarray(lam_deaths_parent, dtype=float) - lam_birth))\n    s_children = float(sum(np.sum(np.asarray(deaths, dtype=float) - b_c) for b_c, deaths in lam_deaths_children))\n    choose_children = bool(s_children > s_parent)\n    return (round(mst_w, 4), round(s_parent, 4), choose_children)\n```"
